Other key characteristics of their rule included: 
- Forced labor - People were required to work long hours under dangerous conditions for no pay;
- Excessive purges – Thousands of intellectuals, religious figures and other ‘non-vanguard’ elements within society were executed or sent into exile;
- Mass deportations - Millions of people were forcibly relocated from urban areas into remote rural communes where they faced further hardship due to lack of resources

